{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Inside it.</b> An earthenware vessel becomes impure only from its airspace (Ḥullin 24)." "<b>Whatever is inside it becomes impure.</b> The vessel goes back and impurifies what is in its airspace." "<b>And it you shall break.</b> This teaches that it has no purification in the mikveh."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:54.848092166Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}